You're probably talking about wizard mode, anyway; you won't get your
own quest artifact ("For a moment, you feel something in your hands,
but it disappears!"), the Amulet of Yendor (you get a cheap plastic
imitation) the Bell of Opening (a normal bell) the Candelabrum (a
candle) or the Book of the Dead (I got a spellbook of blank paper,
perhaps it's a random spellbook) in explore mode. 

You could have tried this out for yourself if you're not certain; that's
what explore mode is *for*. Not for cheating, but for trying things out
you're not certain of. It only becomes cheating when you use it to play
a whole game without dying and with extra wishes *and brag about it as
if you did it normally*.

